All commands here are **to be run during implementation**. Export `CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2 CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=true UV_OFFLINE=true`; use `--test-threads=1` for the bounded oracle tests. Before each check record its question, inputs, expected discriminator and stopping condition in `1.2/checks.json`; the entries below supply those four fields. No performance or training conclusions follow. Write the semantic tests in §§5.3–5.6 before filling the corresponding production bodies, and capture each named command's initial red result against explicit error-returning stubs; then implement and run each group green. If preceding work already satisfies a later test, report that honestly and use the specified temporary negative control to prove the test detects its intended fault.

The shared test module resolves fixture paths explicitly by package: `CARGO_PKG_NAME == "owl"` uses `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR`; `"kaggriculture-engine"` uses its parent. Reject any other package name. Join `tests/fixtures/kaggriculture/grammar-v4-reference.jsonl.gz` to that root. Never search arbitrary fallback paths; the same test source runs in both packages.

### 5.1 Register the compiled module and protect pinned bytes

