  ```

  **Dense execution and capacity (Claude review R4, required, not "if necessary").** Build explicit dense states through the public `Game::from_header` path (serialize a real header/initial state, append hands to the chosen seat's farm and matching private inventories in the serialized JSON, deserialize; no private-field access). Then: (i) a 241-actor seat steps a decoded length-252 program (241 unit frames, 10 market orders, STOP) and the kernel accepts it with the expected JSON; (ii) a 240-actor seat with ample cash steps a decoded program with one HIRE, the kernel executes it, and the next state has exactly 241 actors; the plan for that new state (`plan(241, O, 241)`) masks HIRE at every market position, and `encode` of a two-HIRE action on the 240-actor state rejects with `hire capacity`. This is the end-to-end form of the §4 "241 never becomes 242" argument. (iii) Actor order (R3): on a ≥ 3-hand state give farmer and hands distinct moves and assert each unit moved as its frame ordinal says.

  Add the full unit/market command matrices, EMPTY before/between orders, market0, absent/explicit positive transfers, and insufficient-cash HIREs. Assert decoded JSON first and state effects when economically executable; nonexecution may be expected. Dense actor cases use `Game::from_header` as R4 above requires, matching its explicit-state API (`W:engine_rs/src/lib.rs:1318–1365`); do not touch private fields from the integration test or invent a public mutation API. Test both seats. For HIRE failure, compare plans/programs with the same shape and different bank states: mask admission is unchanged.
- [ ] For selected real replay records, instantiate `Game::new` from each official header and advance using the original recorded joint actions to that `from_step`. Clone the game; step one clone with the original joint action and the other with the selected seat replaced by the new decoded action. Assert exact public/private snapshots, recursive key order, statuses/rewards/done and counters equal. This checks acceptance in the **actual replay state**, not just a decoder-context game; use the comparator discipline at `W:engine_rs/tests/replay_parity.rs:13–45,155–176`. Group selections by episode to avoid restarting from seed for each sample. Do not claim a new full-season action-codec qualification from the selected 64 programs; retained Task 1.1 replays separately continue covering all 2,876 transitions.

