ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/plan.md:61:| C4 | `engine_rs/src/myolie_features.rs` (flat v2 "observation-v5" vector) and the reference model's magic-offset slicing (`features[:, 1027:3827]` …) | R | Isaiah feeds named per-entity tensors into stems. Hard-coded offsets are fragile, and the reference review found the flat encoding loses inventory insertion order and some public configuration facts | Information-preservation oracle: on recorded states, every reference feature value is reconstructible from the new tensors, and the lost facts are now present |
