# Task 1.2 — Kaggriculture Grammar Kernel Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** Port C3 into one typed, checked Rust grammar that supplies the v4 action masks and canonical decoding, preserves recorded reference programs, and feeds the pinned rules kernel without changing its bytes.

**Architecture:** Put the production module in `src/kaggriculture/grammar.rs`, compiled by the root crate through `src/kaggriculture.rs`. An authored integration test in the standalone engine package includes that **same source file** by path and calls `Game::step`; it does not link the root crate into the engine. Export a small validated plan/cursor and factored boolean tables instead of the reference binary DFA. No root → engine dependency is added in 1.2; L4 reopens at the first production engine consumer in 1.3/1.4.

**Tech stack:** Existing pinned Rust toolchain, Cargo, Serde JSON, Python standard-library fixture recorder, pytest for tooling tests, system `gzip` for Rust fixture reads. No Torch, GPU, neural sampler, trainer, ctypes, or new crate is needed for this task.

**Spec:** [rebuild plan](../plan.md) C3 and Tasks 1.1–1.5/2.3 (`:47–113`, `:181–232`); [accepted contract v4](../../../docs/kaggriculture-contract.md) (`docs/kaggriculture-contract.md:164–213`); Task 1.1 [brief](1.1-rules-kernel.md); Task 2.3 v3 at **`/Users/poonszesen/kg-v3/ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/briefs/2.3-action-heads.md:27–108`**. The absolute 2.3 path is intentional: it is in the model worktree, not this branch.

**Owner/reviewer:** Codex implements 1.2; Claude cross-reviews and commits. Claude owns the 2.3 handoff. This is a brief only: its sole current deliverable is this file. All other files and commands below are future implementation work, not changes or checks claimed completed today. The user's one-file instruction takes precedence over writing a cookbook trio in this brief-writing task; the implementation inventory explicitly includes that trio.

**Constraints and stopping condition:** CPU-light, offline, `CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2` for every build; no training or GPU work on the owner's Mac. Keep Isaiah's native buffer/`Result` conventions and I10–I12. Do not edit any retained engine bytes, including its Cargo files. Finish implementation only when the oracle counts, bounds, transition/table tests, kernel acceptance, trim checker and preparation checks below pass, with actual results recorded. Diagnose a failed check before changing its expectation. No commit from this Codex sandbox. Sources: `AGENTS.md:17–20,25–33,80–116,118–160`; `CLAUDE.md:1–184` is the same file through a symlink; `plan.md:13–24,111–137`.

